description:
Canonical mail-client analog of JMAP-wzq9.33 (metadata-client) and sibling-side counterpart to JMAP-1j9k.20 (calendars-client).

## Sites

- `crate-jmap-mail-client/src/methods/email.rs:46`
- `crate-jmap-mail-client/src/methods/identity.rs:36`
- `crate-jmap-mail-client/src/methods/mailbox.rs:39`
- `crate-jmap-mail-client/src/methods/submission.rs:47`
- `crate-jmap-mail-client/src/methods/thread.rs:34`

Each contains:

    if let Some(props) = properties {
        args["properties"] = serde_json::Value::Array(
            props.iter().copied().map(serde_json::Value::from).collect(),
        );
    }

## What idiomatic Rust would do

`serde_json::to_value` on `&[&str]` invokes the `str` Serialize impl on each element and produces `Value::Array(Vec<Value::String>)` — byte-identical wire output to the hand-rolled version:

    if let Some(props) = properties {
        args["properties"] = serde_json::to_value(props)
            .expect("&[&str] Serialize is infallible");
    }

…matches the idiom used 1-3 lines above for the `ids` slice in every one of these files (e.g. email.rs:42):

    if let Some(id_slice) = ids {
        args["ids"] = serde_json::to_value(id_slice).expect("Id slice Serialize is infallible");
    }

## What goes wrong if it stays

Nothing at runtime — both forms produce the same wire JSON. The cost is *clarity and internal consistency*: each `_get` method performs the same slice-to-JSON-array operation two different ways, three lines apart.

## Workspace propagation

Per workspace AGENTS.md "Canonical Templates", fix here first, then propagate to all 7 extension-client siblings:

- metadata-client side: JMAP-wzq9.33 (1 site)
- calendars-client side: JMAP-1j9k.20 (6 sites)
- chat-client, contacts-client, tasks-client, filenode-client, sharing-client: not yet tracked; this canonical-side fix's propagation pass should sweep all 7 siblings in one commit.

